 "text": "Log in\nSubscribe\nHome\nPosts\nWhat you'll walk out with on Monday\nWhat you'll walk out with on Monday\n\nThe 3-Day AI Business Launch Challenge.\n\nAug 13, 2026\n\n•\n\n2 min read\n\nOn Monday we're running the 3-Day AI Business Launch Challenge\n\nOne line of qualification first, so nobody wastes their morning: this is for people who want to get paid to build AI for other businesses. If you run a company and just want AI working inside it, skip to the bottom — there's something built for you there instead.\n\nHere's what it is.\n\nThree days. One decision each day. A deadline at the end.\n\nMost people who want to start an AI business don't have a knowledge problem — there's more free AI content than anyone could watch in a year. They have a decision problem. They've never committed to one buyer, one offer and one way of reaching people, because committing means being wrong in public.\n\nThree days is enough time to make all three decisions if someone holds you to it. That's the entire premise.\n\nWhat you walk out with\n\nOne document — your Launch Audit — answering four questions:\n\nWho you sell to\n\nWhat expensive problem you fix for them\n\nHow much you charge, and on what terms\n\nHow you reach them, starting immediately\n\nThen a human reviews it against a published rubric and either approves it or names the exact sections to fix. Once it's approved, the 90-day roadmap opens up — daily actions with a number attached to each one.\n\nWhat we actually cover\n\nWhich lane to pick — build it, deploy it inside a business, or sell it. Most people stall because they're quietly attempting all three.\n\nHow to choose one market — who signs the cheque, and whether a customer is worth enough for the math to work.\n\nWhich problem is the expensive one, as opposed to the loud one everybody complains about.\n\nWhat to charge, on terms you can say out loud without flinching.\n\nWhat to promise — a guarantee limited to what you actually control.\n\nOne route to buyers, and the 14-day activity number you commit to.\n\nIt works when people actually pick.\n\nNoah picked one offer — an AI receptionist — then searched a job board for businesses already hiring receptionists. People who'd already admitted the problem and posted the budget. A few signed at $1.5k–$2k each. Just over $5,000 in a month, with no ads, no funnel and no portfolio.\n\nChris picked one route — a local networking room — and landed a $2,500 build plus $197/month. Salah picked one specific job and got a six-location restaurant chain as his first client.\n\nI'm not promising you a paying client in three days. That isn't in my control or yours. What is: a market, an offer, a price, a route, and a plan someone has actually checked.\n\nIt runs inside AI Accelerator+ — $72/month, and you need to be a member to take part. Kickoff is Monday.\n\nJoin and be in Monday's cohort\n\n-- Nick\n\nP.S. — for the business owners I flagged at the top. Here's yours. Tell us your revenue, team size and one goal, and you'll get back three systems to build in order, with an honest range on the hours and dollars each gives back. Takes about a minute.\n\nGet your free AI Business Growth Plan\n\nKeep Reading\n\nJul 29, 2026\n\n•\n\n4 min read\n\nAI hasn't paid off in your business yet. Your industry isn't the reason.\n\n$340K at one firm. $210K at another. Two builds with nothing in common.\n\nJul 15, 2026\n\n•\n\n5 min read\n\nRun Your Entire Business With Fable 5\n\nSep 18, 2026\n\n•\n\n1 min read\n\nHow to Start and Scale an AI Agency\n\nA free training on what to sell, how to find clients, and how to close them.\n\nView more\nThe AI Core\n\nThis free newsletter is how you win the AI era.\n\nSubscribe\n© 2026 The AI Core.\nPowered by beehiiv\nLog in\nSubscribe",
